      "storetime": "2180-06-25 01:14:00",
      "text": " \nName:  ___                  Unit No:   ___\n \nAdmission Date:  ___              Discharge Date:   ___\n \nDate of Birth:  ___             Sex:   F\n \nService: MEDICINE\n \nAllergies: \nPatient recorded as having No Known Allergies to Drugs\n \nAttending: ___.\n \nChief Complaint:\nChief Complaint: Hypotension\n \nMajor Surgical or Invasive Procedure:\nHemodialysis x2\n\n \nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ with DM II,paroxismal A-fib on coumadin,diastolic heart \nfailure (EF > 60%), Bil BKA, and ESRD on HD 4x/wk (___) with \nrecent admissions for hypotension and chest pain after HD. Today \npatient had BP of ___ after 2.5hrs of 3hr HD session. She \ndeveloped left sided chest tightness and generalized myalgias \n(back and arm ache). She states that this episode was similar to \nprevious episodes when her BP dropped after dialysis. She denies \nhaving any dizziness, lightheadedness, loss of conscious, or \nshortness of breath during this episode. She had 3 previous \nepisodes of hypotension in the past few months and they have \nchanged her dialyse schedule from 3 to 4 times per week which \nseems to have improved symptoms of hypotension. She denies \nhaving any changes in her medications or diet since she was \ndischarge home in ___. She denies having any episodes of chest \npain/pressure, n/v, dizziness, except for one episode of watery \nbowel movement yesterday and mild back pain this morning which \nresolved with Tylenol. She can not describe location or nature \nof the back pain. She didn't take her BP pills this morning \nprior to dialysis.\n\nShe had 1L fluid replaced at HD. In ED, EJ placed, given 500cc \nbolus, BP improved from ___ to 95/54 (baseline). EKG with \nafib (old), HR 110-> 98, ___ 99RA. Afebrile. Her chest \npain/tightness resolved with IV fluids.\n\nOn arrival to the floor, patient states to be feeling \"\"much \nbetter\"\" improved symptoms of chest tightness. She was sitting in \nno acute distress. Her BP 104/60. \n.  \nOf note, pt was recently discharged ___ after admission for \nsimilar symptoms of chest tightness and hypotensive during HD \n(in the ___ SBP). Her BPs were responsive to IVF boluses in the \nED, and her BP meds were held. Head CT (done for mild mental \nstatus changes initially) was negative. She was ruled out for \nACS by serial ECGs and cardiac enzymes.\""
    }
  ],
  "radiology_notes": [
    {
      "note_id": "12324099-RR-160",
      "charttime": "2180-03-02 10:13:00",
      "storetime": "2180-03-02 10:51:00",
      "text": "INDICATION:  Patient is a ___ female with left back pain and\nhypotension.  Please evaluate for acute process.\n\nEXAMINATION:  Single frontal portable chest radiograph.\n\nCOMPARISONS:  Chest radiograph from ___.\n\nFINDINGS:  A right-sided hemodialysis catheter is seen in stable position with\ntip projecting over the right atrium.  The lungs are clear with no signs of\npneumonia or congestive heart failure.  The visualized cardiomediastinal\nsilhouette is stable in appearance, demonstrating mild cardiomegaly.  The\naorta is tortuous. Redemonstrated are multilevel degenerative changes of the\nthoracolumbar spine. No pleural effusions or pneumothorax is identified.\n\nIMPRESSION:  No acute intrathoracic process.\n"
    }
  ],
